  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are organizing a charity event where people donate various items, and you want to\nkeep track of the number of donated items of each type. You use an array called\ndonationCounts to represent the number of donations of each type, where the value at\neach index corresponds to the count of donations for that type.\nHowever, sometimes multiple people donate the same type of item simultaneously,\nleading to duplicate counts in the array. To rectify this, you decide to increment the\ncount of each duplicate item in the array by 1 until all counts become unique. Each\nincrement operation corresponds to a \"move.\"\nYou are given an integer array donationCounts. In one move, you can pick an index i\nwhere 0 <= i < donationCounts.length and increment donationCounts[i] by 1.\nYour task is to determine the minimum number of moves needed to ensure that each\ntype of donated item has a unique count in the donationCounts array.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= nums.length <= 10^5",
      "-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "3\n1 2 2",
    "outputFormat": "1",
